   ],
   "note": "OQ 59: retyped from `back-hall` to `gallery-corridor`, and the service rooms regrouped into one dependency. A hyphen is a connecting gallery between the block and a wing; a back hall is the service corridor beside a kitchen, and its own hard rule is must_adjoin kitchen by direct door. Typed as back-halls, BOTH hyphens demanded a kitchen at their own end and only one wing has one -- an unsatisfiable requirement produced by naming the room wrongly rather than by drawing it wrongly. The east dependency now holds the library and the west the whole service block, which is what a five-part house does: one wing works and one wing is quiet."
  },
  {
