   "lit_from": [
    "N"
   ],
   "doors": [
    "dining",
    "westhyphen"
   ],
   "fixtures": [
    "sink"
   ],
   "note": "OQ 59: moved into the main block beside the dining room, which is where a butler's pantry is once it exists at all -- it is the room that keeps the dining room from touching the kitchen, and in a five-part house the kitchen is a separate building. It reaches the kitchen through the hyphen, which is the same principle the corpus already states about the butler's pantry itself: the named intermediary is the connection, not a failure to connect."
  },
